# Displaying Forms in Templates 🖼️

## View

```python
from .forms import ContactForm

def contact(request):
    form = ContactForm()
    return render(request, 'contact.html', {'form': form})
```

## Template Rendering Options

```html
<form method="post">
    {% csrf_token %}

    <!-- Option 1: Auto render all -->
    {{ form.as_p }}     <!-- Wrapped in <p> tags -->
    {{ form.as_table }} <!-- As table rows -->
    {{ form.as_ul }}    <!-- As list items -->

    <!-- Option 2: Manual control -->
    {{ form.name.label_tag }}
    {{ form.name }}
    {{ form.name.errors }}
    {{ form.name.help_text }}

    <button type="submit">Submit</button>
</form>
```

## Styling with CSS Classes

```python
class ContactForm(forms.Form):
    name = forms.CharField(
        widget=forms.TextInput(attrs={
            'class': 'form-control',
            'placeholder': 'Enter your name'
        })
    )
```

> ⚠️ **Always include `{% csrf_token %}` in POST forms!** It protects against CSRF attacks.

# Validation ✅

## Processing Form Submissions

```python
def contact(request):
    if request.method == 'POST':
        form = ContactForm(request.POST)
        if form.is_valid():
            # Data is validated and cleaned
            name = form.cleaned_data['name']
            email = form.cleaned_data['email']
            # Process data...
            return redirect('success')
    else:
        form = ContactForm()

    return render(request, 'contact.html', {'form': form})
```

## Custom Field Validation

```python
class ContactForm(forms.Form):
    email = forms.EmailField()

    def clean_email(self):
        email = self.cleaned_data['email']
        if not email.endswith('@company.com'):
            raise forms.ValidationError('Must use company email')
        return email
```

## Cross-Field Validation

```python
class SignupForm(forms.Form):
    password = forms.CharField(widget=forms.PasswordInput)
    confirm_password = forms.CharField(widget=forms.PasswordInput)

    def clean(self):
        cleaned_data = super().clean()
        password = cleaned_data.get('password')
        confirm = cleaned_data.get('confirm_password')

        if password != confirm:
            raise forms.ValidationError('Passwords do not match')
        return cleaned_data
```

# ModelForms 🔗

Automatically create forms from models!

## Basic ModelForm

```python
from django import forms
from .models import Article

class ArticleForm(forms.ModelForm):
    class Meta:
        model = Article
        fields = ['title', 'content', 'category']
        # Or use: fields = '__all__'
        # Or exclude: exclude = ['author']
```

## Customizing ModelForm

```python
class ArticleForm(forms.ModelForm):
    class Meta:
        model = Article
        fields = ['title', 'content']
        labels = {
            'title': 'Article Title',
        }
        widgets = {
            'content': forms.Textarea(attrs={'rows': 10}),
        }
        help_texts = {
            'title': 'Enter a descriptive title',
        }
```

## Saving ModelForm

```python
def create_article(request):
    if request.method == 'POST':
        form = ArticleForm(request.POST)
        if form.is_valid():
            article = form.save()  # Saves to database!
            return redirect('article_detail', pk=article.pk)
    else:
        form = ArticleForm()
    return render(request, 'create.html', {'form': form})
```

> 💡 **ModelForms are the recommended way to create/edit model instances!**
